# Oasis Tasks - Deep Work Manager

A functional task management dashboard built with Vanilla JavaScript, HTML, and CSS. This project focuses on high-contrast UI design and real-time DOM manipulation to enhance cognitive flow and productivity.

## 🚀 Key Features
* **Dynamic Task Management**: Add new tasks to the workflow instantly.
* **Interactive UI**: Toggle task completion status by clicking on task cards, providing immediate visual feedback.
* **Live Progress Tracking**: A real-time progress bar and counter that calculates completion percentage based on your active tasks.
* **Responsive Layout**: A triple-column dashboard designed for deep work environments.

## 🛠️ Technical Implementation
* **DOM Manipulation**: Utilizes `document.createElement` and `appendChild` to manage task lifecycles without page reloads.
* **Event Delegation**: Implements a single event listener on the parent task list to handle clicks on dynamically created items efficiently.
* **CSS Transitions**: Smooth animations for the progress bar and task card interactions to improve user experience.

## 📁 Project Structure
* `index.html`: Main application structure.
* `style.css`: Rugged, industrial-inspired UI styling.
* `script.js`: Core logic for task handling and progress calculations.
* `/prototypes`: Contains Lo-Fi wireframes and Hi-Fi designs used during the planning phase.

## 📖 How to Run
1.  Clone this repository to your local machine:
    ```bash
    git clone [https://github.com/nejj0002/final-js-task-manager.git](https://github.com/nejj0002/final-js-task-manager.git)
    ```
2.  Open `index.html` in any modern web browser.
3.  Alternatively, use the **Live Server** extension in VS Code to view real-time changes.

## 🎓 Academic Context
This project was developed as a Final Project for the Interactive Media & Design program. It demonstrates core competencies in Vanilla JavaScript, DOM manipulation, and UX/UI design principles.